From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:36:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: take the MLO station rates from the links
 that report them

cfg80211_sta_set_mld_sinfo() takes the TX and RX rate of an MLO station
from the link with the least inactive time. The inactive time block
before it has already stored this link's value as the least one when it
is, so the comparison against it never holds after the first link. The
first link then decides alone, and where that link reports no rate the
station reports none.

mac80211 records the last TX rate of a driver with its own rate control
on the station's default link, which is the association link. A station
that associated on any other link than the first therefore reports no
TX bit rate at all: an MLO backhaul station associated on link 1 of a
mac80211_hwsim AP MLD shows only the RX rate of link 0.

Track the least inactive time per rate among the links that report it.
The TX and RX durations had the same condition, so only the first link
was counted; sum them over every link.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 net/wireless/nl80211.c | 21 ++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

--- a/net/wireless/nl80211.c
+++ b/net/wireless/nl80211.c
@@ -8295,6 +8295,7 @@ static void cfg80211_sta_set_mld_sinfo(s
 	struct link_station_info *link_sinfo;
 	int link_id, init = 0;
 	u32 link_inactive_time;
+	u32 txrate_inactive_time = U32_MAX, rxrate_inactive_time = U32_MAX;
 
 	sinfo->signal = -99;
 
@@ -8421,31 +8422,27 @@ static void cfg80211_sta_set_mld_sinfo(s
 		/* Update MLO rates as per last updated link rate */
 		if ((link_sinfo->filled &
 		     BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_BITRATE)) &&
-		    (!init ||
-		     link_inactive_time > link_sinfo->inactive_time)) {
+		    link_sinfo->inactive_time <= txrate_inactive_time) {
+			txrate_inactive_time = link_sinfo->inactive_time;
 			sinfo->txrate = link_sinfo->txrate;
 			sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_BITRATE);
 		}
 		if ((link_sinfo->filled &
 		     BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_BITRATE)) &&
-		    (!init ||
-		     link_inactive_time > link_sinfo->inactive_time)) {
+		    link_sinfo->inactive_time <= rxrate_inactive_time) {
+			rxrate_inactive_time = link_sinfo->inactive_time;
 			sinfo->rxrate = link_sinfo->rxrate;
 			sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_BITRATE);
 		}
 
 		if (link_sinfo->filled &
-		    BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_DURATION) &&
-		    (!init ||
-		     link_inactive_time > link_sinfo->inactive_time)) {
+		    BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_DURATION)) {
 			sinfo->tx_duration += link_sinfo->tx_duration;
 			sinfo->filled |=
 				BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_DURATION);
 		}
 		if (link_sinfo->filled &
-		    BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_DURATION) &&
-		    (!init ||
-		     link_inactive_time > link_sinfo->inactive_time)) {
+		    BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_DURATION)) {
 			sinfo->rx_duration += link_sinfo->rx_duration;
 			sinfo->filled |=
 				BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_DURATION);
